00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.570
So, Yale had a strong
commitment to liberal arts

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.953
education as we all know.

00:02:25.243 --> 00:02:27.061
And part of it is the
foreign language requirement.

00:02:27.061 --> 00:02:31.760
That means that every
student who comes to Yale

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.040
has to take a foreign language.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.760
It doesn't matter what their
level in a certain language is.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.490
They can choose to take a new language.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.820
They can decide to expand their knowledge

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.303
in an existing language.

00:02:45.814 --> 00:02:46.910
But, in any event, each and
every one of them is taking

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.493
at least one course in a foreign language.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.920
Hebrew, as many other languages

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.050
that were presented here today,
Arabic included, and Korean,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.222
of course, is what is called the less,

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:03.050
or considered the less
commonly taught language.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.330
That means that we don't,
unlike the more commonly taught

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.100
languages, Spanish, for example,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.237
I always blame them for everything.

00:03:10.237 --> 00:03:14.717
We do not have very good textbooks.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:20.390
So, we have to glean our
pedigogical materials

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.680
from different sources.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.393
And, this is where Canvas
is very, very effective.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.284
There's one other issue,

00:03:28.284 --> 00:03:31.220
and this, I will have
to actually look at it,

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.760
and this is the difficult level

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.520
of foreign languages in general.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.830
There is a division we should
took it with a grain of salt,

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.650
but generally speaking, Hebrew belongs

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:45.960
to a category four level language.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.261
And that is, the division was made by the

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.410
Foreign Service Institute

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.810
of the U.S. Department of the State.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.770
And that means that in order
to achieve an advanced level,

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.910
advanced meaning actual
scale, and it's called an RS

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.910
in their scale, a student needs
of have 1100 contact hours

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.850
in the language.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.290
Now, if you do a simple
math, because this is all

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.757
that I am capable of
being from the humanities,

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:23.757
at Yale, we teach five hours
a week for, say 26 weeks,

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:27.800
if we exclude exams and things like that.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.940
But, this is actually include those hours,

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.066
so that's 130 hours a year.

00:04:32.066 --> 00:04:35.750
Lets say that the student
is highly committed,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.090
and they take eight
semesters of the language.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:41.850
We're still even less than
half of where we should be

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:45.405
in order to have them reach that level.

00:04:45.405 --> 00:04:50.070
That means that we really
need to rely on homework,

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:53.265
and on work done outside of classroom.

00:04:53.265 --> 00:04:58.179
And to that end, I want
to just show how we use,

00:04:58.179 --> 00:05:01.473
in the Hebrew program, we use Canvas.

00:05:01.473 --> 00:05:04.720
And again, I credit Orit
for this beautiful idea

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.200
of dividing courses into weeks.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.420
So students, yes, they do have to count,

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.739
but only to 13.

00:05:12.739 --> 00:05:16.350
And therefore know when
they are in each week,

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.600
but once we press, they
have all the work that they

00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:23.819
need to do, it's also
convenient for me if I want to

00:05:23.819 --> 00:05:27.250
embed and show certain clips in classes.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.640
I don't have to go back to my
email and get it from there.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.710
I just click and it's there.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:37.259
And then, at the end of every
class, it's always in green,

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:40.053
because that's kind of how I like.

00:05:41.426 --> 00:05:42.259
And, it's not as intimidating as red.

00:05:43.458 --> 00:05:45.390
They press and they have
list of everything they need

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.473
to do for homework.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.976
No, that's not that.

00:05:48.976 --> 00:05:51.465
Why is it significant?

00:05:51.465 --> 00:05:53.710
Because here you can see,
they have six different

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.300
homework assignments.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:59.243
And they need to know
where to get things from.

00:05:59.243 --> 00:06:02.690
And, when we have everything in one place,

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:05.660
they just click and get
to where they need to be.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.822
So, it functions very
much like the modules,

00:06:07.822 --> 00:06:12.822
only it incorporates many other sources.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:16.603
Yeah, I'm good.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.940
In addition to sending
them to specific website,

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.350
I also here, send them to
the specific assignments

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.250
that they need to respond to.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:38.250
And here I will end with
just one minor complaint,

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.269
last one.

00:06:39.269 --> 00:06:43.950
Because they have to basically
submit even different things

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.610
for each class, sometimes they don't do

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:47.960
those things at once.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:52.960
The problem is that when
they upload the material,

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.100
they need to upload everything together,

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.050
so if they have seven files, for example,

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.080
if we sent them to do some
online activity and then

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.380
I asked them to do a
screenshot of the activity,

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.200
so that I know that
they've done it, and also,

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.020
what went wrong, what was good, et cetera,

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.190
they have to submit everything at once.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.340
Because if they do it in
two times, for example,

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.510
the first time gets erased.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.993
So, we do need something.

00:07:18.486 --> 00:07:22.730
We need something else for
them, improve and take care of.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:27.730
Other than that, been working
with Canvas for two years,

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:29.843
I do like it.

00:07:29.843 --> 00:07:30.830
I don't tell Kimberly that,

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:35.010
but it is much more convenient,
and straight forward

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:39.380
once you get the hang
of it than class V2 was.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.760
And the team is highly professional,

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.538
and responsive to the
extent that they can.

00:07:45.538 --> 00:07:49.930
So, at least they will hear
you complain about things,

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.897
and say, "Yes, yes, we are working on it.

00:07:51.897 --> 00:07:54.080
"We promise to make it better."

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:54.913
Thank you.

